<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8b22759ce852c64e6b7accd13d93233e043d9560" commit="10286bc1a814f2953c7e12952b3ea1fdf84f42de" commit_message="vpd: Generalized replacement for block_devmode_vpd.  Old script allowed to enable or disable block_devmode in VPD. The new script allows to do the same to any flag and supports multiple flags in the input.  To be used by login_manager::VpdProcessImpl.  BUG=chromium:438234 TEST=Tested manually in console CQ-DEPEND=CL:336438, CL:344511  Change-Id: I8b22759ce852c64e6b7accd13d93233e043d9560 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/336357 Commit-Ready: Igor Covganet &lt;igorcov@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Igor Covganet &lt;igorcov@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Thiemo Nagel &lt;tnagel@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="336357" owner_email="igorcov@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform/vpd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vpd" ref="refs/changes/57/336357/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib6e884969532515f20a1060cdd000831a467a86d" commit="47a8c88878097d4665227b3f5225f385ce7cf517" commit_message="login: VPD update implemented as part of policy store.  The policy store flow in Chrome OS part starts in SessionManagerDBusAdaptor::StorePolicy() method.  The old implementation was using a DBusMethodCompletion object to pass to SessionManagerImpl and to PolicyService, so that whenever an error occurs or the process is finished, the completion object is used to notify Chrome through DBus call about the flow result.  The object is destroyed when the function call is finished and it checks in destructor that the completion object was used. See DBusMethodCompletion::HandleResult from SessionManagerDBusAdaptor and its destructor.  Chrome considers that enrollment is done when it receives the response through DBus call from that object.  Since VPD update is running in a separate process, we need to know when the process finishes. So, the VpdProcessImpl was converted to be a JobManagerInterface and we are notified when the process is finished through HandleExit method.  Since the VPD update is the last step in the flow of policy store, the VpdProcessImpl object will run the completion when it finishes. This will send the D-Bus response back to Chrome.  The functionality to update VPD was moved to DevicePolicyService class and additional cc file was added for dbus_error namespace so that the constants inside act can be passed between methods.  BUG=chromium:438234 TEST=manually tested only lumpy device and unit tests. CQ-DEPEND=CL:336357, CL:344511  Change-Id: Ib6e884969532515f20a1060cdd000831a467a86d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/336438 Commit-Ready: Igor Covganet &lt;igorcov@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Igor Covganet &lt;igorcov@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Thiemo Nagel &lt;tnagel@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="336438" owner_email="igorcov@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="39" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/38/336438/39" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5b604296c1095fd59d483924ad34fb1801261e22" commit="69bc2406797210871db23571dd09428d94cfddc5" commit_message="vpd: New script to replace block_devmode_vpd  Changed the script name to be used for VPD update in login_manager::VpdProcessImpl.  BUG=chromium:438234 TEST=Tested manually in console CQ-DEPEND=CL:336438,CL:336357  Change-Id: I5b604296c1095fd59d483924ad34fb1801261e22 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/344511 Commit-Ready: Igor Covganet &lt;igorcov@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Igor Covganet &lt;igorcov@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Thiemo Nagel &lt;tnagel@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="344511" owner_email="igorcov@chromium.